</programlisting></para>
<para>Interestingly, the analytical solution to this model approaches a Gaussian distribution with zero mean, and variance <formula id="112">$\Sigma^2=\frac{\sigma^2}{2\Gamma}$</formula>. We can therefore compare our distributions (blue) to the analytical soltuion (orange) over time, as shown in the images below.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>The analytical solution is only valid if all particles are driven by independent Wiener processes; for a shared process, the variance is zero, and the distribution collapses into a Dirac-delta distribution that moves randomly about the mean.</para>
</simplesect>
